# {{properCase game}}: picks, panels and the table

The visual contract this UI keeps, in the sections `docs/ui-interaction-visual-contract.md` requires. Every intent names the rule it serves; every scenario says how it is checked.

## Visual intents

- **<Intent name> (R-x.y):** what the player sees while the intent is active, what is emphasised, what is dimmed, what stays unaffected, and what each press does.

## Coexistence and precedence

- Which intents can be active together, and which one wins where they meet.
- What the Undo control unwinds, in order: manual draft entries first, then the last committed action.

## Shared visual state

| State | Producer | Consumers | Lifetime | Validity |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

Lifetime says when the state disappears (`updatingVisibleState`, `resetAction()`, Undo). Validity says whether a surviving value is still allowed under the current state. History view and replay show none of it.

## Render ownership

- Which layer owns each visual, and what it reads.
- Where fixed overlays mount, outside transformed ancestors.
- Motion: which actions animate, through `AnimationContext`, and what reduced motion does.

